    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Documentation:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Capture detailed photos of the vehicle highlighting any damages or discrepancies. Include close-up shots of any significant areas to ensure a comprehensive record.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Verification against LR Bill of Lading:</strong> Compare the actual vehicle's odometer reading with the recorded odometer reading mentioned in the LR Bill of Lading. Ensure that both values match, confirming that the vehicle has not been tampered with or understated during transit.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Documentation:</strong> Record and document the verification process, including both the current odometer reading and the recorded reading from the LR Bill of Lading. This record can be used as proof in case of any future disputes.</span></li>
</ul>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Conducting Inspection:</strong> Before signing off on the vehicle's condition, conduct a thorough inspection of the vehicle with the recipient or designated person present. This ensures transparency, accountability, and allows for any potential concerns to be addressed.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Documentation:</strong> Compile a detailed report summarizing the inspection findings, including any damages, scratches, or missing parts. Include a clear and precise description of each issue and its severity. Include photos for further clarification and evidence.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signature Exchange:</strong> Before signing off the condition, ensure that the recipient or designated person signs the document, acknowledging their inspection and agreement with the findings. This signed document should be retained by both parties as proof of the inspection process.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>By following these steps, the destination delivery handover for Two-Wheeler &amp; Motorcycle vehicles becomes more secure and transparent. These measures not only protect the interests of the shipper but also ensure that the recipient receives the vehicle in the agreed-upon condition.</p>

<p>It is essential to perform these tasks during daylight conditions, as it allows for a thorough inspection and reduces the chances of misunderstanding the vehicle's condition.</p>

<p>When conducting the inspection, it is crucial to pay close attention to all aspects of the vehicle, including the body, tires, wheels, engine, and any additional parts or accessories.</p>

<p>Documentation is a crucial component of this process. Detailed descriptions and photos should be provided, clearly highlighting the damages or discrepancies discovered during the inspection.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



